    "notes": "F-023 is specifically the whole-project deletion atomicity gap. The implementation adds one project-store operation that opens a single readwrite transaction spanning both the projects and image-assets object stores, deletes matching project assets and the project record inside that transaction, and updates the main deletion and failed-import cleanup paths to call that canonical operation. Existing DB/schema constants remain unchanged; F-032 storage ownership duplication is reviewed but intentionally not remediated here. Full-system discovery surfaces that reference main.js/projectStore.js and their architecture, module, persistence, renderer, placement and historical documentation paths are explicitly acknowledged without semantic changes. No Item/BOM, placement, renderer, catalog, project schema, or import archive format semantics are intentionally changed."
  },
  "tests": {
